+## Unreleased (scenes fork 0.8.6.56)
+
+### New Features
+
+- **Table feed and `table-watch`**: follow a session in real time. The module records the table (chat, rolls, combat turns, player token moves, doors, hit points, players joining) and the server sends one bundled "beat" on `ws://127.0.0.1:31418` only when the GM is needed: a player writing as their character or privately to the GM, a GM-run creature's turn, a door opening, or all awaited rolls coming in. Public out-of-character and blind messages do not wake it. Beats carry a table snapshot. Timings are adjustable; a module setting mutes it. `request-player-rolls` makes the feed wait for that roll.
+- **`get-character` playState** (dnd5e): classes, proficiency, initiative, speed, senses, saves, spell DC and attack, spell slots left, hit dice left, feature and item uses left with their recovery, death saves, exhaustion, concentration, legendary actions.
+- **`combat attack` checks**: refuses targets out of reach or range (`ignore_range` to roll anyway), rolls with disadvantage beyond normal range, and warns when it is not the attacker's turn or someone is already at 0 hp.
+- **Tokens by name**: `move-token`, `update-token` and `get-token-details` accept a token or actor name as well as an id; ambiguous names are refused with the candidates.
+
+### Fixes
+
+- `list-creatures-by-criteria` returned no CR and marked every creature as not undead; it now reports CR, HP, AC and the type flags from the creature index.
+- Layouts are kept in a per-user data folder (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\FoundryMCPServer\layouts` on Windows; `FOUNDRY_MCP_LAYOUTS_DIR` overrides it) instead of the temp folder, which clean-ups can empty. Layouts from the old folder are copied over once.
+- The combat readout showed a stale Bloodied right after healing; it is now derived from the hit points.
+
